      "recommendation": "Do not push yet; add one adversarial orchestration test proving that an ordinary direct child of sourceCommit is rejected, then tighten both lineage checks until that test passes while a canonical @semantic-release/git release commit remains accepted.",
      "rationale": "Parentage alone proves only that gitHead immediately follows sourceCommit; it does not prove the child was created by @semantic-release/git. Accepting every direct child therefore weakens the stated invariant and could admit an unrelated commit. The smallest safe correction is to distinguish the configured release commit using independently validated release-commit characteristics, such as its expected commit message and permitted changed paths, while retaining exact parent and single-parent checks. This preserves provenance without changing release contracts or bypassing verification.",
      "must_fix": [
        "Reject a direct child that is not demonstrably the configured @semantic-release/git release commit.",
        "Apply identical acceptance criteria in the release-candidate and publisher paths.",
        "Add explicit tests for sourceCommit equality, a valid single-parent release child, an unrelated direct child, a non-child commit, and a merge commit."
      ],
      "cautions": [
        "Commit-message matching alone is forgeable and insufficient; combine it with exact parentage and an allowlist of changes derived from canonical @semantic-release/git configuration.",
        "The supplied excerpts do not contain the modified verifier or new tests, so the implementation cannot be assessed for SHA validation, merge-parent handling, command failure behavior, or consistency between scripts.",
        "The reported 52 passing tests demonstrate regression coverage but do not establish that arbitrary direct children are rejected."
      ],
      "assumptions": [
        "@semantic-release/git is canonically configured with deterministic commit-message and asset-path settings.",
        "The release workspace and sourceCommit are already authenticated by existing release-contract checks.",
        "The verifier resolves full commit objects and treats missing or malformed commits as failures."
      ],
      "success_checks": [
        "A valid sourceCommit is accepted unchanged.",
        "A single-parent child matching the canonical release-commit shape is accepted.",
        "An ordinary direct child of sourceCommit is rejected.",
        "A merge commit containing sourceCommit as one parent is rejected.",
        "Malformed, abbreviated, missing, and unrelated commit identifiers fail closed.",
        "npm run test:release reports 32/32, and npm run release:check plus npm run distribute:check both exit 0."
      ],
      "unresolved_questions": [
